untain stream texture preserved\n@Video1: Motion reference, replicate the full sword-swinging and aerial spinning martial arts movement trajectories from the video\n@Audio1: Background music reference, fully reuse the ancient Chinese instrumental track dominated by bamboo flute with beat-aligned drum rhythm\nCore Concept\nAn aloof white-robed xianxia maiden (@Image1) practices swordsmanship on stone steps in a misty bamboo forest at dawn. Eastern ink wash cinematic style with epic atmosphere, continuous composite orbiting one-shot camera movement, golden hour soft glow with Tyndall light beams through woods, high-contrast teal & orange film color grading.\nScene Breakdown & Visual Sequence\n0–4s [Extreme Long Shot → Full Shot, Continuous Push-In]\nVisual content: Rolling mist shrouds endless bamboo mountains; the maiden walks slowly into frame from distant stone steps, surrounded by thin mountain haze\nCamera movement: Combined crane up + slow push-in. Camera rises from ground to 8 meters high, advancing forward gradually at 12cm/s over 6 seconds, keeping the subject centered as visual anchor\nMotion breakdown: Light footsteps on stone slabs → upright steady walking posture → left hand hanging naturally, right hand lightly gripping sword hilt, hem of robe fluttering gently in mountain wind\nLighting setup: Warm golden side backlight at 45° as key light, bright white rim light outlining hair strands and robe edges, cool cyan ambient fill light softening shadows, 8:1 high contrast ratio, suspended mist particles forming visible Tyndall light columns\nAudio layers: Rustling wind through bamboo as ambient base tone, soft footsteps on bluestone, bamboo flute intro from @Audio1 plays in sync\nEnvironmental feedback: Bamboo leaves sway layer by layer in wind, mountain mist drifts slowly, tiny ripples spread across stream surface, mild airflow from the maiden’s steps disperses haze in front of her face\nNo dialogue\n4–9s [Medium Full Shot + Orbiting Camera]\nVisual content: The maiden halts at the center of stone steps, draws her sword and performs a complete sword dance; sword aura stirs countless green bamboo leaves flying all around\nCamera movement: Orbiting shot centered on the character with 3-meter radius, rotation speed 28°/s, slight inward push simultaneously for composite orbit-push lens\nMotion breakdown: Right hand lifts hilt upward to draw sword (metallic buzzing friction sound) → both hands grip sword overhead for opening stance → wide downward slash toward lower left → side spin half-turn mid-air → horizontal sword sweep → land steadily and settle stance; airflow from sword aura swirls massive amounts of bamboo leaves into the air\nLighting setup: Warm key light brightens the maiden’s front, cool cyan ambient light fills the bamboo background, faint cyan self-glow emanates from the sword blade, light spots scatter across bamboo leaf surfaces\nAudio layers: Metallic sword-drawing friction, cutting wind from sword swings, rustle of falling bamboo leaves, drum beats from @Audio1 sync with heavy sword strikes\nEnvironmental feedback: Dozens of bamboo leaves lifted and spinning mid-air by sword airflow, tree trunks shake slightly under air impact, tiny water splashes blown up from mountain stream, hair strands fly backward following spinning movement\nNo dialogue\n9–12s [Close-Up Locked Static Shot, Closing Frame]\nVisual content: Maiden sheathes sword and lowers her gaze, standing quietly amid bamboo with fallen leaf resting on her shoulder\nCamera movement: Stop orbiting, fixed focus close-up, camera remains completely static\nMicro-expression & subtle motions: Gentle chest rise and fall with steady breathing, slow eyelash drop, slightly lowered jaw, fingertips resting lightly on scabbard, bamboo leaf slides slowly off shoulder\nLighting setup: Soft diffused ambient glow, faint halo wrapping around the character, background bamboo forest softly blurred via shallow depth of field\nAudio layers: Wind fades gradually, bamboo flute melody eases to a gentle close, low resonant hum from metal sword blade\nEnvironmental feedback: Remaining airborne leaves drift slowly to ground, mountain mist drifts back to converge, stream ripples fade away gradually\nNegative Exclusion Instructions\nNon-diegetic background music: N/A, only @Audio1 soundtrack used throughout. No modern buildings, artificial digital special effects, cartoon stylization, random passersby, gory exaggerated combat, distorted facial features, messy text or watermarks.\nAdvanced Additional Camera Parameters\nComposition: Rule-of-thirds framing throughout, character anchored at lower-right cross visual point. No Dutch tilt, no shaky handheld footage. No hard cuts, full unbroken one-shot without frame interruption. 85mm telephoto lens with blurred distant background to highlight the main character via shallow depth of field."], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "value"}, "name": "value", "label": "value", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "值"}], "flags": {}, "type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline", "title": "Input Text (Prompt)", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#533", "size": [370, 390], "pos": [-1480, 6000], "id": 138, "properties": {"ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "input_ue_unconnectable": {}, "version": "7.8"}, "widget_ue_connectable": {"value": true}, "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveStringMultiline"}, "order": 2}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#222", "widgets_values": ["| megapixels | Aspect | Output (multiple=32) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0.2 | 16:9 | 608 x 352 |\n| 0.3 | 16:9 | 736 x 416 |\n| 0.4 | 16:9 | 864 x 480 |\n| 0.5 | 16:9 | 960 x 544 |\n| 0.6 | 16:9 | 1056 x 608 |\n| 0.7 | 16:9 | 1152 x 640 |\n| 0.8 | 16:9 | 1216 x 672 |\n| 0.9 | 16:9 | 1280 x 736 |\n| 0.98 | 16:9 | 1344 x 768 |\n| 1.0 | 16:9 | 1376 x 768 |\n| 1.2 | 16:9 | 1504 x 832 |\n| 1.5 | 16:9 | 1664 x 928 |\n| 1.8 | 16:9 | 1824 x 1024 |\n| 2.0 | 16:9 | 1920 x 1088 |\n"], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "MarkdownNote", "title": "Note: Size Settings Reference", "mode":